 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` (`src/tessel/cli.py:380`). It loads the app and pushes its app context around your callback. Use it with a plain `@click.command()`, as `shell_command` and `routes_command` do.\n\nIf you register the command with `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()`, you don't need it. `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`) wraps the callback in `needs_app_scope` automatically, and you can opt out with `needs_app_scope=False`.\n\n**Loader:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`). `LaunchInfo.load_app()` (line 333) imports and caches the app, using `create_app`, the `--app` import path, or `wsgi.py`/`app.py`. `TesselGroup` (line 531) creates it for the `tessel` command, and `needs_app_scope` calls it through `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo).load_app()`. Under the hood, `locate_app`/`find_app_by_string` do the discovery.",
